Keep an explicit --bfbs-comments working with -b --schema.

flatc's per-generator option loop assigns binary_schema_comments from
CodeGenerator::SupportsBfbsGeneration(), which is false for the plain
binary generator, so 'flatc --bfbs-comments -b --schema foo.fbs' emitted
a .bfbs without any documentation. OR the flag in instead of overwriting
it. Tools that read doc comments out of the reflection schema depend on
them, so losing them is a behavior change, not just cosmetic.
--- a/src/flatc.cpp
+++ b/src/flatc.cpp
@@ -788,7 +788,13 @@
         opts.lang_to_generate |= code_generator->Language();
 
         auto is_binary_schema = code_generator->SupportsBfbsGeneration();
-        opts.binary_schema_comments = is_binary_schema;
+        // Don't clobber an explicit --bfbs-comments: this assignment runs for
+        // every requested generator, and plain binary schema output
+        // (`-b --schema`) reports SupportsBfbsGeneration() == false, which
+        // silently dropped the user's flag and stripped documentation from
+        // the emitted .bfbs.
+        opts.binary_schema_comments =
+            opts.binary_schema_comments || is_binary_schema;
         options.requires_bfbs = is_binary_schema;
         options.generators.push_back(std::move(code_generator));
       }
